<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>CSS Selectors Practice</title>
    <style>
        #main-banner {
            height: 200px;
            width: 100%;
            border: 10px solid black;
            background-color: gold;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
        .info-box {
            width: 200px;
            height: 100px;
            padding: 20px;
            margin: 10px;
            background-color: lightblue;
            display: inline-block; 
            vertical-align: top;
        } 
        p {
            font-size: 20px;
            border-left: 10px solid red;
            color: darkgrey;
            padding-left: 10px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Task1 </h1>
    <div id="main-banner">
        Welcome to the Identity Banner
    </div>
    <h1>Task2 </h1>
    <div class="info-box">Status Card 1: Processing...</div>
    <div class="info-box">Status Card 2: Active</div>
    <div class="info-box">Status Card 3: Complete</div>
    <h1>Task3 </h1>
    <p>Hello World! This is the first global paragraph.</p>
    <p>Notice how every single paragraph gets the red left border.</p>
    <p>Changing the 'p' selector updates all of these at once.</p>
    <p>Standardized text styling made easy!</p>

</body>
</html>
